  "notes": "Grades are named by Hebrew letters: kita aleph (Grade 1) to kita yud bet (Grade 12). Some schools keep an older 8-4 split (elementary to Grade 8) and some six-year schools run Grades 7-12; grade names are the same. Arabic-language schools use Arabic grade names (e.g. الصف الأول), not recorded here. Both gov.il sources block this network; their content was read from Internet Archive copies (Jan 2026 and May 2025)."
